Managed K8S cluster
IN K8S managed means control plane will be managed by cloud providers

Pre-requisites:

EC2
IAM role
kubectl
eksctl


Create an ec2 instance and assign the role to it.
Install eksctl and kubectl

create EKS cluster and nodes from ec2 management tool
#eksctl create cluster --name cluster-name --region region-name --node-type instance-type --nodes-min number --nodes-max number --zones <az-1>,<az-3>

#eksctl create cluster --name my-lab-cluster --region ap-south-1 --node-type t2.medium

eksctl create cluster --name my-lab-cluster --region ap-south-1 node-type t2.small --nodes 1 --node-volume-type standard --node-volume-size 20 --spot

#eksctl delete cluster my-lab-cluster --region ap-south-1


$ kubectl get nodes
